.TH FLAMQUENCY 1 "October 2026" "flamquency-sync 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
flamquency \- terminal-based file synchronization with version control
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B flamquency
[\fI\,COMMAND\/\fR] [\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
FlamQuency-Sync is a terminal-based file synchronization tool with real
version control, snapshots, and one-click rollback. It stores every version
of your files in content-addressable blob storage (compressed, optionally
encrypted with Fernet/AES), can back up to a local folder, GitHub, any
S3-compatible service, SMB/NFS shares, or Google Drive and Dropbox via
rclone, and offers both a Textual TUI and a scriptable CLI.
.PP
Besides plain sync, v2.0 adds scheduling (cron / Task Scheduler), smart
autosync with a quiet period, post-sync hooks, and a self-learning layer
(\fBevolve\fR) that watches how you work and suggests improvements.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B sync
Synchronize files according to configuration. Follows the active profile,
an explicit \fB\-\-profile\fR, or a single \fB\-\-source\fR.
.TP
.B status
Show current sync status: last sync, backend, tracked files, encryption,
active profile.
.TP
.B snapshots
List available snapshots.
.TP
.B rollback
Rollback the whole system to a snapshot (\fB\-\-list\fR to see them).
.TP
.B rollback-file
Rollback a specific file to a chosen version.
.TP
.B restore-content \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-version\fR N] [\fB\-\-output\fR PATH]
Restore the content of one version to any path, leaving the original alone.
.TP
.B view-content \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-version\fR N] [\fB\-\-max-bytes\fR N]
Print a version's content without restoring anything.
.TP
.B restore-tree [\fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR NAME] [\fB\-\-output\fR DIR]
Restore a whole directory, a profile, or the entire store at one version.
.TP
.B diff \fIFILE\fR \fB\-\-v1\fR N \fB\-\-v2\fR N
Diff two versions of a text file, colour-coded, with an added/removed count.
.TP
.B stats [\fB\-\-graphs\fR] [\fB\-\-by-type\fR] [\fB\-\-top\fR N]
Storage statistics: dedup ratio, saved space, per-type bar chart,
top-changed files, and a storage growth sparkline.
.TP
.B check
Verify blob store integrity.
.TP
.B prune
Prune old snapshots with restic-style retention (\fB\-\-keep-last\fR,
\fB\-\-keep-daily\fR, \fB\-\-keep-within\fR, \fB\-\-dry-run\fR).
.TP
.B profile
Manage sync profiles: named sets of paths (list, create, delete, use,
show, add-path, remove-path, describe).
.TP
.B ignore
Manage \fI~/.flamquencyignore\fR: glob rules plus global \fB\-\-size-gt\fR /
\fB\-\-size-lt\fR / \fB\-\-types\fR rules. \fB\-\-check\fR PATH explains which
rule decided.
.TP
.B backend
Manage storage backends: \fBlist\fR, \fBcheck\fR, \fBuse\fR. Secrets live in
environment variables, never in the config.
.TP
.B schedule [\fIINTERVAL\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR NAME] [\fB\-\-remove\fR]
Set up a recurring sync. Accepts human intervals ("каждый час",
"каждые 30 минут", "daily") or a raw cron expression.
.TP
.B evolve [\fB\-\-apply\fR] [\fB\-\-decay\fR] [\fB\-\-forget\fR PATH...]
Self-learning layer: shows or applies suggestions (hot files, new profiles,
shortcuts) based on how you work.
.TP
.B spark
Quick actions in one command (\fBset\fR, \fBremove\fR, \fBshow\fR,
\fB\-\-list\fR, \fB\-\-dry-run\fR). Three are built in.
.TP
.B echo [\fB\-\-add\fR N]
Read your shell history and suggest paths worth syncing. Everything is
computed locally.
.TP
.B kaleido [\fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-random\fR]
Colour variations of the "Угольки" theme.
.TP
.B encryption
Manage blob encryption: status, enable, disable, change-password.
.TP
.B update [\fB\-\-check\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
Check for and install updates from GitHub.
.TP
.B watch
Watch directories and auto-sync on changes (smart quiet period).
.TP
.B config [\fB\-\-edit\fR]
Show or edit configuration.
.TP
.B help [\fICOMMAND\fR]
Detailed help: what a command is for, live examples, related commands.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-profile, \-P \fINAME\fR
Sync this profile instead of the active one (sync, restore-tree, schedule).
.TP
.B \-\-password, \-p
Blob store password (else the FLAMQUENCY_PASSWORD environment variable).
.TP
.B \-\-source, \-s \fIPATH\fR
Sync a single directory, bypassing profiles.
.TP
.B \-\-yes, \-y
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Preview an action without performing it.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.flamquency/config.yaml
User configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.flamquencyignore
gitignore-style exclusion rules, plus size/type rules.
.TP
.I ~/.flamquency/sync/
Local sync destination.
.TP
.I ~/.flamquency/versions/blobs/
Content-addressable compressed blob storage.
.TP
.I ~/.flamquency/versions/files/
Per-file version history.
.TP
.I ~/.flamquency/snapshots/
Snapshot manifests.
.TP
.I ~/.flamquency/schedule.json
The schedule FlamQuency believes is installed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FLAMQUENCY_PASSWORD
Blob store password, so scripts never prompt.
.TP
.B FLAMQUENCY_S3_ACCESS_KEY, FLAMQUENCY_S3_SECRET_KEY
S3 credentials (only when the s3 backend is active).
.TP
.B FLAMQUENCY_GITHUB_TOKEN
GitHub token for the github backend.
.TP
.B FLAMQUENCY_SMB_USER, FLAMQUENCY_SMB_PASSWORD
SMB share credentials.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Sync everything:
.B flamquency sync
.TP
Read what a file looked like two versions ago:
.B flamquency view-content notes.md \-\-version 1
.TP
Restore a whole directory into a scratch folder first:
.B flamquency restore-tree docs \-\-output /tmp/проверка
.TP
Rollback a single config file:
.B flamquency rollback-file ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.conf \-\-version 2
.TP
Schedule an hourly sync of one profile:
.B flamquency schedule "каждый час" \-\-profile work
.TP
Never sync files over a gigabyte, or any video:
.B flamquency ignore \-\-size-gt 1GB \-\-types mp4,avi,mkv
.TP
See what the self-learning layer suggests:
.B flamquency evolve
.TP
Launch the TUI:
.B flamquency-tui
